-- ownership: calls (`ownership-checker.md` §6.1, and since slice 2 §16.4).
-- Slice 1 had no summaries and made a call's result a fresh list plus every
-- argument list its type could hold; slice 2 reads the same verdicts off
-- the callees' inferred summaries. `List.filter xs p : List Int` is a
-- fresh list, `res fresh` — since the owner dropped the identity promises
-- on 2026-10-13 (`ownership-checker.md` §27) it never returns `xs` itself —
-- so extending it while `xs` is read later is accepted, `call` (T52's
-- shape, rejected until then through `res fresh, π1`).
-- `List.map xs String.fromInt : List String` is fresh too: the extension
-- is accepted, `call`. `List.length` returns an `Int`, which crosses and
-- holds nothing. `[ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]` reads a fresh temporary while
-- writing `xs`, so Disjoint holds and it is accepted, `param` (it was
-- rejected as `call`, through `reverse`'s promise for fewer than two
-- elements).
pub filtered : List Int → Int
filtered xs =
    kept = List.filter xs λx → x > 0
    grown = [ …kept, 0 ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub mapped : List Int → Int
mapped xs =
    labels = List.map xs String.fromInt
    grown = [ …labels, "end" ]
    List.length grown + List.length xs


pub counted : List Int → List Int
counted xs =
    n = List.length xs
    [ …xs, n ]


pub mirrored : List Int → List Int
mirrored xs = [ …xs, …List.reverse xs ]
